    "steps": [
      { "text": "Heat the oven to 200°C and line a roasting tin with baking paper." },
      { "text": "Toss the carrot batons with 1 tbsp of the olive oil, spread them out in the tin and roast for 25 minutes, turning once, until the edges catch and darken." },
      { "text": "Meanwhile, simmer the lentils in a generous pan of water for 20–25 minutes, until tender but still holding their shape, then drain well." },
      { "text": "Whisk the remaining 2 tbsp of olive oil with the vinegar, cumin and chili flakes in a wide serving bowl." },
      { "text": "Tip the warm lentils and carrots into the dressing and leave them for 5 minutes to drink it in." },
      { "text": "Scatter over the spring onions and parsley, season with sea salt to taste, and toss gently before serving." }
    ],
    "notes": "Warm lentils soak up dressing far better than cold ones, so dress them the moment they are drained.",
